# The graphs this model composes, as the lane sets of one pool. One row per graph: what its nodes
# are, what its edges are, and what a cycle in it means.
#
# A `VALUES` literal, because it is a contract
#   Derived from the tree it could never report that a graph has nothing behind it, and the
#   claimant row is exactly that case: it is declared here and supplies no edges at all, which is
#   the finding rather than an omission.
#
# Three lane sets, not three lanes
#   A `laneSet` is a partition claimed exhaustive, so three lanes would put every composition in
#   exactly one, and most compositions touch more than one graph: a relation reading a part and its
#   factor is in the layer graph and the unit graph, and that is what a factor is. BPMN permits
#   several lane sets over one process for exactly this reason.
#
# Only one can be the containment
#   An inclusion tree gives each node one parent, so only one of these can be the nesting a diagram
#   draws; the others need showing some other way. That is why `examples/diagramming/main.rs`
#   takes the graph as a slot rather than picking one silently, and why a caller that names none
#   does not run.

# ⛔ `cycle_sense` exists because the word has four referents in this tree
#   This relation asks one question, "what does a cycle in it mean", of three graphs, and without
#   this column it was answered in two different senses. The four are set out in
#   `composition/descent.sqlc`'s header: undirected, which is a SUBSPACE at dimension `m - n + c`;
#   directed, which is a PARTITION of the nodes into the classes of `F+ ∩ (F+)ᵀ`; a duty cycle,
#   which is a RATIO and not a graph object at all; and the loop you can walk, which is what the
#   other three compose to. A column that does not say which is not comparable across its own
#   rows, which is the only thing a three-row contract read by one emitter is for.
#
# The layer row answers the UNDIRECTED sense, and it used to answer the directed one
#   Both are true of the layer graph and they are not interchangeable. `checks/layers_move_together`
#   rules on the directed sense, the classes of mutual reachability. `checks/jagged_layer` is what
#   holds the UNDIRECTED dimension at zero, which `algebra/cycle_space` states as
#   `dim ker B = 0 ⟺ |jagged| = 0` and `examples/graphs/main.rs` asserts on every run. A diamond
#   separates them: it is acyclic as a digraph, so nothing is mutually reachable and
#   `layers_move_together` finds nothing, while its cycle space is `4 - 4 + 1 = 1` and
#   `jagged_layer` accuses. ⛔ This column answers the undirected sense because that is the one the
#   drawing itself carries: `examples/diagramming/main.rs` computes the emitted call graph's
#   `m - n + c` and holds it against the model's.
#
# `governed_by` is now checked against what actually holds the dimension
#   It used to have to RESOLVE and nothing more, so a graph could cite any relation in the tree
#   and the emitter would carry the citation into a reader's document. `examples/graphs/main.rs`
#   now holds each graph to the rule it uses itself.
-- the three graphs this model composes, as data an emitter chooses between.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('layers',    'a layer, keyed (filing, layer)', 'a part: F : layer -> layer',
                'undirected',
                'a leaf reached down two branches of one fold, which is a double count rather than a partition',
                                                                              'checks/jagged_layer'),
  ('units',     'a unit',                          'a conversion: phi : unit -> unit',
                'undirected',
                'expected, and required to close: the weights on it must vanish, so a potential exists',
                                                                              'checks/conversion_cycle_does_not_close'),
  ('claimants', 'a claimant: software, an agent, a role, a person',
                'delegation, and nothing files it',
                'directed',
                'unknown. Not "nobody is accountable": mutual signing authority is a legitimate cycle',
                                                                              NULL)
) AS g(graph, node_is, edge_is, cycle_sense, a_cycle_is, governed_by)
